ile extension. Direct curl verification attempted twice (default UA and a full Chrome/Windows UA string) and both returned HTTP 403 -- legifrance.gouv.fr's known recurring anti-bot block, same failure mode as iterations 21/27's France citations -- so the two independent WebFetch quotes were accepted as sufficient primary-source verification, consistent with that established precedent. clojure -M:test run in the child repo checkout before writing (28 tests baseline) and again after landing, both directly in the working branch and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 32 tests / 120 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via throwaway branch add-fra-knitwear-epr -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1430/merges, commit dd84773a1c8f86c3abcec02041a3e70d4e595994) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/knitwear/facts.cljc + test/knitwear/facts_test.clj touched) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 6188f5b5b609 -> dd84773a1c8f (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was a deliberate return to an already-verified catalog, per the established fallback pattern -- see event/action).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis to restore balance after iteration 28's prod-ready landing. Axis alternation is now 14 prod-ready / 15 real-world-ingest-gap across 29 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 29, :event/at "2026-07-22T03:55:00Z"}
