{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 31, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-3530", :event/action "Added Germany (:DEU) as a 4th jurisdiction to steam.facts/catalog (was JPN/USA/GBR/FRA), the last-touched-in-iteration-3 catalog. Chose AVBFernwärmeV (Verordnung über Allgemeine Bedingungen für die Versorgung mit Fernwärme) -- Germany's national general-terms-of-supply ordinance specific to district-heat networks -- for a genuinely distinctive angle not represented by any existing entry: a PROCEDURAL/PROPORTIONALITY safeguard on payment-delinquency disconnection under §33(2) (a 2-week notice period following a warning/dunning notice, waivable if the customer shows disconnection would be disproportionate to the violation's severity AND there is sufficient prospect of future compliance), distinct from JPN/USA's flat :allowed-true suspension shape and FRA's connection-obligation-penalty shape. Modeled via a new :notice-and-proportionality-safeguard sub-map under :suspension-requirements plus a notice-period-days-for helper (with a test explicitly asserting JPN has no such safeguard modeled, to make the distinction machine-checkable). Also added §2 (written-contract/free-disclosure-of-supply-conditions) and §24 (billing/price-change-clause transparency) as :requirements entries.", :event/verification "Initial WebSearch attempt failed (this session's 200/200 WebSearch budget, confirmed still exhausted); fell back to the established curl-based DuckDuckGo-HTML-redirect-extraction technique, which also caught a wrong first guess -- gesetze-im-internet.de/avbfernwv/ 404'd, the DDG search surfaced the correct slug avbfernw_rmev instead. Unlike legifrance.gouv.fr, gesetze-im-internet.de has NO anti-bot blocking in this session's environment (consistent with prior German-citation iterations, e.g. iteration 1's EnWG) -- direct curl succeeded (HTTP 200) and the full primary-source ordinance text (all 37 paragraphs) was read directly via pandoc, including §2, §24, and §33 verbatim, no WebFetch fallback needed. clojure -M:test run in the child repo checkout before writing (18 tests baseline) and again after landing, both directly in the working branch and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 23 tests / 72 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via throwaway branch add-deu-steam-avbfernwaermev -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-3530/merges, commit 0f7ec1ba759a4c23b98b751386db0170c90325de) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/steam/facts.cljc + test/steam/facts_test.clj touched) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 6f284d9e30a1 -> 0f7ec1ba759a (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. Also proactively found and fixed a stale loop-system-dynamics pin (89ec8c243d31 -> c7732c7039a6, confirmed ahead_by 1 / behind_by 0 via compare API before patching).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was a deliberate return to an already-verified catalog, per the established fallback pattern).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis. Axis alternation is now 15 prod-ready / 16 real-world-ingest-gap across 31 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 31, :event/at "2026-07-22T05:20:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 32, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-brn", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Brunei Darussalam (BRN) from a src/culture-only stub, same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/28/30. Delegated implementation to a background agent (isolated worktree clone, never touched the shared checkout or main), briefed to compare closely against Barbados (BRB, most recently completed) and Belize (BLZ), and specifically instructed to investigate rather than assume Brunei's genuinely unusual fiscal system (no personal income tax) and dual civil/Syariah legal-system split. Delivered: marketentry.facts (Brunei's procurement is gazette/notice-based, not portal-based -- correctly discovered and disclosed that tender notices are published in Pelita Brunei, the official government newspaper, via mofe.gov.bn, rather than assuming a modern e-procurement portal exists; procurement value-tier thresholds under the Financial Regulations (Small Value <=$2,000 / Quotations $2,000-$50,000 / Open Tender >$50,000 / Selective Tender Mini/STB $50k-$500k / >$500k); ROCBN (Registry of Companies and Business Names Division) under MOFE as company registrar; Income Tax Act Cap. 35 confirming 18.5% corporate rate (2015+) and, genuinely distinctively, Schedule 1(a)'s express exclusion of individuals from the tax's scope -- Brunei has NO personal income tax, independently confirmed via primary-text read rather than assumed) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: a pure precedence/ordering check (plain ISO-8601 `compare`, no arithmetic and no threshold at all -- distinct from Bulgaria's %-formula, Albania's flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia's boolean membership, Antigua and Barbuda's 3-tier class, Benin's bid-margin recompute, Belize's struck-off boolean, Barbados's expiry-date recompute): Companies Act Cap. 39 Part 9 ss.298/299/306 require a foreign-incorporated company to lodge Registrar-of-Companies registration BEFORE establishing a place of business or commencing business in Brunei (s.306: $1,000 fine + $25/day continuing offence for non-compliance), implemented as an entity-scope-gated check (a no-op unless :foreign-company? is true, since Part 9 only applies to foreign-incorporated companies by the Act's own s.298). Statute.facts: Employment Act Cap. 278 (Commissioner of Labour), Business Names Act Cap. 92, Personal Data Protection Order 2025 (Authority = AiTi). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing (4 items): rep-spec-basis left nil (could not fetch/read the Financial Regulations' own primary text, an access gap rather than a negative finding); did not claim a named 'e-perolehan'-style portal exists -- narrowed to what was actually verified (gazette/notice-based); the 55% oil/gas petroleum tax rate cited only from MOFE's FAQ page, not the Income Tax (Petroleum) Act's own primary text, flagged as lower confidence than the 18.5%/no-personal-tax findings; did not independently confirm which sections the Personal Data Protection Order's two commencement notices (S 10/2025, S 11/2025) actually activate. Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md found in several prior siblings' repos.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Companies Act Cap. 39 PDF myself (agc.gov.bn, ~10MB) and read ss.298/299(1)/306 directly -- exact match: s.298 defines Part 9's scope (companies incorporated outside Brunei), s.299(1) requires lodgement with the Registrar 'before it establishes a place of business or commences to carry on business', s.306 confirms the exact '$1,000 ... or, in the case of a continuing offence, $25 for every day' penalty; (2) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Income Tax Act Cap. 35 PDF myself and independently found both cited provisions -- the 18.5% corporate rate ('the year of assessment 2015 and subsequent years of assessment upon the chargeable income of every company, tax at the rate of 18.5 per cent') and, separately, Schedule 1(a)'s exact text ('Tax shall be charged, levied and collected only in respect of the incomes of companies... and the provisions of the Act shall not have effect in respect of incomes of any other persons or bodies of persons') confirming no personal income tax; (3) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain} for :local/root resolution) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 37 tests / 124 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 37/124/0; (4) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (5) grepped the merged repo for cambodia/khmer/iso3166-khm leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture, test/culture, schema/, data/ untouched via diff --stat; (6) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 18 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (7) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-brn checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch agent/scaffold-market-entry-actor-2026072200 -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-brn/merges, commit 775e6c537ab8925dc9ff403e0d5f52a02c689476) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 48fe693cd06d -> 775e6c537ab8 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- kept pace on the prod-ready axis to restore balance. Axis alternation is now 16 prod-ready / 16 real-world-ingest-gap across 32 iterations, evenly balanced.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 32, :event/at "2026-07-22T06:35:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 33, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1410", :event/action "Added United Kingdom (:GBR) as a 5th jurisdiction to apparel.facts/catalog (was VNM/BGD/USA/IND). Initial research attempt targeted China's GB 18401-2010 textile chemical-safety standard for a genuinely new requirement category (finished-garment chemical composition, not manufacturing-process/labor/labeling/tariff), but the official SAMR national-standards platform (openstd.samr.gov.cn / std.samr.gov.cn) turned out to be a JS-driven search UI that WebFetch/curl cannot execute (the same class of limitation hit for e-qanun.az/qbz.gov.al/law.go.kr in iterations 4/5/6), and this session's curl-DuckDuckGo search fallback also started returning DDG's own anti-bot 'anomaly' challenge page (a new limitation, not previously hit this session) rather than usable results -- so China/GB18401 was abandoned honestly rather than forced through a weaker secondary-source-only citation. Pivoted to the SAME chemical-safety requirement category via a more directly-fetchable jurisdiction/source: UK REACH (retained Regulation (EC) No 1907/2006) Annex XVII Entry 43 (Azocolourants and Azodyes), which restricts azo dyes that release listed aromatic amines above 30 mg/kg (0.003% by weight) in textile/leather articles with direct skin/oral-cavity contact, and separately caps listed azodyes at 0.1% by weight when used for textile/leather coloring. This is the catalog's first chemical-safety/restricted-substances requirement, genuinely distinct in kind from VNM/BGD/USA/IND's plant-registration/labor-standards/quality-labeling/tariff-compliance/fiber-content shape (all of which regulate the manufacturing process or disclosure, not the finished garment's chemical composition).", :event/verification "legislation.gov.uk (The National Archives' official UK legislation site) was fetched directly via plain curl with NO anti-bot blocking whatsoever (HTTP 200) -- a cleaner verification path than several prior France/China-targeting attempts this session. The exact restriction text (Entry 43's paragraph 1 threshold language, Appendix 8's aromatic-amines list, Appendix 9's azodyes list) was read directly from the fetched primary text, not summarized by an intermediary. clojure -M:test run in the child repo checkout before writing (25 tests baseline) and again after landing, both directly in the working branch and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 29 tests / 118 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via throwaway branch add-gbr-apparel-reach-azodyes -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1410/merges, commit 36b11b05f8c4b50bbe57b86558a182c6364394c8) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/apparel/facts.cljc + test/apparel/facts_test.clj touched) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 1cda0abce6c9 -> 36b11b05f8c4 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None new this iteration (China/GB18401 was abandoned for tooling-access reasons, not because it was a false positive -- it remains a plausible, not-yet-attempted future candidate if a JS-capable browsing tool becomes available; logged here so a future iteration does not re-attempt the exact same JS-SPA path without a different tool).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis. Axis alternation is now 16 prod-ready / 17 real-world-ingest-gap across 33 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 33, :event/at "2026-07-22T07:00:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 34, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-btn", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Kingdom of Bhutan (BTN) from a src/culture-only stub, same pattern as iterations 2/4/5/8/10/12/28/30/32. Delegated implementation to a background agent (isolated worktree clone, never touched the shared checkout or main), briefed to compare closely against Brunei (BRN, most recently completed) and specifically instructed to investigate Bhutan's distinctive FDI-restriction framework as a candidate for a genuinely new flagship-check shape. Delivered: marketentry.facts (e-GP e-procurement portal at egp.gov.bt, legal basis Public Finance Act 2007 s.104(i) as amended by the Public Finance (Amendment) Act 2012, per the Procurement Rules and Regulations 2025's own preface; Companies Act of Bhutan 2016 establishing the Regulatory Authority / Registrar of Companies (= CRA, cra.gov.bt); Department of Revenue and Customs (DRC) TPN registration via RAMIS) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: a pure SET-MEMBERSHIP / sector-eligibility gate (no dates, no arithmetic, no supplier-registry read at all -- distinct from every prior sibling: Bulgaria %-formula, Albania flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia boolean supplier-registry membership, Antigua and Barbuda 3-tier class, Benin bid-margin recompute, Belize struck-off boolean, Barbados expiry-date recompute, Brunei precedence-ordering check): is the engagement's declared :fdi-sector a member of the FDI Rules and Regulations 2025's Schedule III Negative List (9 enumerated activities: News Media, Distribution Services, Standalone Mineral Sale, Mineral Processing, 3-Star-and-Below Hotels, General Health Services, non-Certificate-of-Origin-compliant industries, Real Estate, and the Prohibited List), entity-scope-gated on Rule 138(12)'s 'FDI Company' definition (>=20% foreign equity, or >=10% for foreign institutional investors). Statute.facts: Companies Act of Bhutan 2016, Labour and Employment Act of Bhutan 2007, Public Finance Act of Bhutan 2007. Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing (3 items): rep-spec-basis left nil -- found the real Debarment Rules 2023 (Anti-Corruption Commission, under Anti-Corruption Act 2011 ss.40(3)/171) but its debarment-duration clause (Rule 54) rendered only in Dzongkha prose the agent could not fluently read, so only the English portions actually read were cited, not the duration; did not assert a separate legal instrument renamed 'Registrar of Companies' to 'Corporate Regulatory Authority' -- the Companies Act 2016's own text only says 'Regulatory Authority'; did not fetch/read the GST Act's own primary text, only named it from DRC's listing page. Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md found in several prior siblings' repos.", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Companies Act of Bhutan 2016 PDF myself (oag.gov.bt, ~10.6MB) at the EXACT URL cited in the repo (not a guessed one -- an initial guessed URL 404'd, so the actual cited URL was extracted from the repo's own facts.cljc first) and read s.387 directly -- exact match: 'The Office of the Registrar under this Act is hereby established as an autonomous Regulatory Authority'; (2) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the FDI Rules and Regulations 2025 PDF myself (industry.gov.bt) and independently found both cited provisions -- Schedule III's exact 9-item Negative List (verbatim match down to each activity name) and Rule 138(12)'s exact 'FDI Company' definition text ('20% or more of the equity... owned by foreign investors... 10% or more of the equity is owned by foreign institutional investors'); (3) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Income Tax Act of Bhutan 2025 PDF myself (drc.gov.bt) and confirmed both ss.296/299 exist with TPN-application-duty language; (4) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain} for :local/root resolution) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 38 tests / 127 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 38/127/0; (5) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (6) grepped the merged repo for cambodia/khmer/iso3166-khm leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture, test/culture, schema/, data/ untouched via diff --stat; (7) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 19 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (8) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-btn checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch agent/btn-marketentry-actor-scaffold -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-btn/merges, commit 826fd57cbc5aadb89313920d0525dceb41b7418c) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 8fea2d8ee859 -> 826fd57cbc5a (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- kept pace on the prod-ready axis to restore balance. Axis alternation is now 17 prod-ready / 17 real-world-ingest-gap across 34 iterations, evenly balanced.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 34, :event/at "2026-07-22T08:15:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 35, :event/axis :real-world-ingest-gap, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-isic-1512", :event/action "Added Japan (:JPN) as a 5th jurisdiction to luggage.facts/catalog (was USA/ITA/CAN/MEX). Citation: the Household Goods Quality Labeling Act (家庭用品品質表示法, Act No. 104 of 1962) Art. 1-3 plus its Enforcement Order (家庭用品品質表示法施行令, Cabinet Order No. 390 of 1962) Appended Table item 11, which designates 'かばん' (bags, limited to those made of cowhide or other Cabinet-Office-Ordinance-designated material) as a household good subject to the Act's Article 3 standardized quality-labeling regime set by the Prime Minister. This adds a genuinely distinctive two-tier statute-plus-delegated-Cabinet-Order legal mechanism (the Act itself designates NO specific product; the actual item-by-item designation, including leather bags, lives entirely in the Enforcement Order's Appended Table) alongside the same conceptual 'quality-labeling' category USA/CAN/MEX already model.", :event/verification "e-Gov's newer elaws.e-gov.go.jp/document UI turned out to be a JS-rendered SPA that returns only an empty app shell to direct curl (confirmed: HTTP 200 but 800-byte response containing only a <div id=\"app\"> mount point and script tags, no law text) -- a new instance of the same class of JS-SPA limitation hit for e-qanun.az/qbz.gov.al/law.go.kr in iterations 4/5/6 and openstd.samr.gov.cn in iteration 33. Worked around by using e-Gov's own underlying law-data API (laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/1/lawdata/<law-id>), which returns the full law text as XML directly -- located the Act's own law-id via WebSearch-alternative reasoning from a prior citation pattern, then found the Enforcement Order's separate law-id via e-Gov's law-list API (laws.e-gov.go.jp/api/1/lawlists/1) filtered for the Act's own name plus '施行令'. Both the Act's Article 1/2 text and the Enforcement Order's Appended Table item 11 (naming かばん explicitly) were read directly from the fetched primary XML text via a Python regex-strip, not summarized by an intermediary. clojure -M:test run in the child repo checkout before writing (30 tests baseline) and again after landing, both directly in the working branch and independently in a SEPARATE fresh clone of merged main: 34 tests / 116 assertions, 0 failures in every run. Landed via throwaway branch add-jpn-luggage-quality-labeling -> push -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-1512/merges, commit e71fcc7a5e8564e38b35da01ead95280e21dd7df) -> diff-scope-verified via compare API (only src/luggage/facts.cljc + test/luggage/facts_test.clj touched) -> branch deleted -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 3c47c1708fad -> e71fcc7a5e85 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins), done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). SEPARATELY, discovered and fixed a real git anomaly in the shared superproject checkout during this iteration's sync step: `git status --short --branch` reported 'ahead 4, behind 3' on main (a genuine-looking divergence), and `git merge-base main origin/main` failed outright (exit 1, no output) -- diagnosed via the established GitHub-API-compare protocol (never trust local ancestry judgment alone) rather than force-syncing blindly: `gh api .../compare/<local-main-tip>...<origin-main-tip>` confirmed a clean pure-forward relationship (merge_base_commit == local main's own tip, behind_by 0), proving this was a shallow-graft false positive, not a real force-push/divergence. Root cause: a `.git/shallow` file had reappeared in the shared checkout (timestamped today) despite ADR-2607211600's full-history-by-default policy -- fixed via `git fetch --unshallow origin`, which removed the shallow marker and repaired local ancestry resolution (`git merge-base --is-ancestor` then correctly returned 0), after which the previously-blocked `git merge --ff-only origin/main` succeeded cleanly with no data loss. Logged here since this exact shallow-graft-reappearance failure mode was previously thought fully closed by ADR-2607211600 but has now recurred at least once since that policy reversal -- a future iteration hitting the same symptom should not assume real divergence and should follow this same GitHub-API-compare-first, then-unshallow-if-confirmed-false-positive sequence rather than escalating or force-pushing.", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (target was a deliberate return to an already-verified catalog, per the established fallback pattern).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No prod-ready stub-scaffold attempted this iteration -- kept pace on the cheaper real-world-ingest-gap axis. Axis alternation is now 17 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 35 iterations.", :event/superproject-adr "adr-2607211900-cloud-itonami-actor-substrate-maturity-loop-charter", :event/seq 35, :event/at "2026-07-22T08:45:00Z"}
{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 36, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-bwa", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for Botswana (BWA) from a src/culture-only stub, same pattern as prior prod-ready iterations. This iteration marks a WORKFLOW CHANGE per explicit owner instruction ('subagent で効率的に深化を進めてください' -- use subagents to advance the deepening efficiently): rather than one agent per iteration processed strictly sequentially, this and the following prod-ready iteration were dispatched as part of a 6-country PARALLEL batch (BWA + CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV launched concurrently as separate background agents), each independently verified and landed as its own completion notification arrives, rather than waiting for each to finish before starting the next. Delivered for BWA: marketentry.facts (Public Procurement Act, 2021 (No. 24 of 2021) governing procurement, replacing PPADB with the Public Procurement Regulatory Authority (PPRA) effective 14 April 2022, National eProcurement System under s.55, IPMS portal at ipms.ppadb.co.bw; Companies Act CAP 42:01 s.10 (Registrar) for company registration via CIPA; BURS Act CAP 53:03 + Income Tax Act CAP 52:01 for tax registration via BURS) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: an ORDERED TIER-CLASSIFICATION recompute (citizen-preference-tier + reservation-ineligible?), independently classifying an engagement's declared citizen-ownership/joint-venture/subcontractor-association facts against the Public Procurement Act 2021 s.78(1)'s exact 4-tier descending preference scale ((a) JV between citizen contractors, (b) sole citizen contractors, (c) JV citizen+local majority-citizen, (d) association arrangements citizen-subcontractor+local-contractor), gated on s.76(1)'s default citizen-reservation rule -- distinct from every prior sibling (Bulgaria %-formula, Albania flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia boolean registry membership, Antigua and Barbuda 3-tier VALUE class, Benin bid-margin recompute, Belize struck-off boolean, Barbados expiry-date recompute, Brunei precedence-ordering, Bhutan sector SET-membership) since this is an ORDERED-TIER classification over a fixed enumerated scale, not a threshold/boolean/date/set-membership check. Statute.facts and PPA text fetched via genuine Wayback Machine captures of ppadb.co.bw after live connections were refused from this network (a real, disclosed access limitation, not fabricated content). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing (6 items, the most of any iteration so far): Employment Act omitted entirely (mlha.gov.bw refused connections, no Wayback snapshot found, WebSearch budget exhausted, DDY curl-fallback hit anti-bot wall); CIPA's own establishing Act cited only to CIPA's self-description, not independently fetched; rep-spec-basis nil; BURS's specific P36,000/P1,000,000 thresholds cited only to BURS's webpage, not independently located in the Income Tax Act's own primary text; IPMS portal's in-portal requirements not modeled (JS-loading-shell-only, no readable content); PPRA's full CEEP/EDD/LPS price-preference percentage matrix read but deliberately not modeled in the pure function (stated scope limitation).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) independently confirmed ppadb.co.bw is genuinely unreachable from this environment myself (curl timeout, HTTP 000), corroborating rather than just trusting the agent's Wayback-Machine-workaround claim; (2) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Companies Act CAP 42:01 PDF myself (cipa.co.bw, live, ~2MB) and read s.10 (Registrar) and s.345 (external companies, local-agent duty) directly -- exact text match on both; (3) re-fetched the Public Procurement Act 2021 PDF myself via the EXACT Wayback Machine URL cited in the repo (not a guessed one) and independently located and read ss.76(1)/77/78(1) body text (the TOC-only grep initially failed to find these sections' body text since the PDF's body headings use a different column-offset format than the TOC listing -- located via the confirmed working format from s.55's body text first) -- exact verbatim match on both s.76(1)'s blanket reservation default and s.78(1)'s precise 4-item descending tier list; (4) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 39 tests / 133 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 39/133/0; (5) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (6) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself -- found intentional comparative 'Bhutan' mentions in facts.cljc/registry.cljc, inspected each and confirmed all are legitimate cross-sibling comparative docstring text (explaining the flagship check's novel shape relative to Bhutan's), not copy-paste errors, matching the established sibling-family documentation convention; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (7) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 14 marketentry/statute/test files and zero culture-catalog/doc files (this repo's docs were already Botswana-correct pre-existing content, unlike some prior siblings); (8) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bwa checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch feat/bwa-market-entry-actor -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-bwa/merges, commit c7e7167383945f1a47975d4d2aea3a6861111c67) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 7f441c354281 -> c7e716738394 (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init