{:event/type :actor-substrate/iteration, :event/iteration 37, :event/axis :prod-ready, :event/repo "cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod", :event/action "Scaffolded the full marketentry + statute governed-actor for the Democratic Republic of the Congo (COD) from a src/culture-only stub, second landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA/CAF/COD/COG/COM/CPV) dispatched per owner instruction to use subagents for efficient parallel deepening. Delivered: marketentry.facts (Loi n°10/010 du 27 avril 2010 relative aux marches publics, grounding ARMP (Art. 14, a posteriori regulation) and DGCMP (Art. 13, a priori control) as the two-authority procurement-oversight split; live e-procurement portal at armp-rdc.cd/marche.armp-rdc.cd plus a real debarment/blacklist page at armp-rdc.cd/liste-noire/; DRC's OHADA membership (ratified 27 June 2012, in force 12 September 2012) confirmed independently rather than assumed from Benin's precedent; company registration via GUCE (Guichet Unique de Creation d'Entreprise, decree n12/045 + arrete n035/CAB/MIN/J&DH/2013); DGI (tax) created by Decret n17/2003 amended by Decret n22/52) + a genuinely new flagship-check SHAPE for this family: a RANKED-CLASSIFICATION recompute against Art. 37's exact 6-tier nationality/ownership preference order (1. Congolese natural person, 2. Congolese-majority-owned SME, 3. Congolese legal person, 4. groupings with Congolese partners/subcontracting, 5. foreign person/entity active in DRC, 6. foreign person/entity from a treaty-partner state) -- distinct from every prior sibling (Bulgaria %-formula, Albania flat threshold, Azerbaijan/Armenia/Bolivia boolean membership, Antigua and Barbuda 3-tier VALUE class, Benin bid-margin recompute, Belize struck-off boolean, Barbados expiry-date recompute, Brunei precedence-ordering, Bhutan sector set-membership, Botswana ordered-tier classification against a 4-item scale) since this is a 6-tier ranked classification against a distinct DRC-specific enumerated order (a similar STRUCTURAL shape to Botswana's ordered-tier check landed earlier in this same batch, but grounded in genuinely different, independently-verified DRC-specific content, not copied). Correctly did NOT model DRC's own Art. 61 discretionary foreign-subcontracting variant (30% subcontract-to-Congolese-firm or 40% Congolese-expert threshold, capped at but not fixed to 5% abattement) -- honestly narrower, mirroring Benin's own prior scope-narrowing discipline on its structurally similar discretionary-margin provision. Statute.facts: OHADA AUSCGIE (independently re-verified: adopted 30 Jan 2014, in force 5 May 2014, NOT copied from Benin's citation text), Code du Travail (Loi n15-2002 amended by Loi n16/010 du 15 juillet 2016). Honest, disclosed scope-narrowing: the specific law/decree creating the NIF tax-ID obligation itself (JS-SPA-blocked); DGCMP's own creation-decree number; INSS's founding law; Art. 37/61's discretionary abattement percentages; any populated blacklist entries (mechanism confirmed real, no specific entity claimed). Also fixed the same class of pre-existing Cambodia/khm copy-paste-template leftover text in CONTRIBUTING.md/GOVERNANCE.md, and independently caught that a stale 'anapi.org' reference in earlier research was actually a hijacked/spam domain -- the real, live ANAPI is anapi.cd (a genuine due-diligence catch, not something merely assumed).", :event/verification "Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session, not just the delegated agent's self-report: (1) re-downloaded and pdftotext-confirmed the Loi n10/010 PDF myself (armp-rdc.cd, 185KB, 31pp) and read Art. 13 (a priori control), Art. 14 (a posteriori regulation body), Art. 37 (flagship), and Art. 61 (foreign-subcontracting discretionary margin) directly -- Art. 37's exact 6-item list matched verbatim, and Art. 61's exact cap language ('abattement qui ne pourra etre superieure a cinq pourcent') confirmed precisely why the agent correctly declined to model it as a fixed value; (2) independently cloned the pushed branch into a fresh isolated tree (symlinked kotoba-lang/{langgraph,langchain}) and re-ran clojure -M:dev:test myself: 37 tests / 131 assertions / 0 failures, matching the agent's report exactly; re-ran again from a SEPARATE fresh clone of the already-merged main tip: same 37/131/0; (3) re-ran clojure -M:lint myself: 0 errors / 8 warnings, matching exactly; (4) grepped for cambodia/khmer/other-sibling-country leftovers myself: none found; confirmed src/culture/test/culture/schema/data/ untouched via diff --stat; (5) confirmed via GitHub compare API against the correct pre-merge parent that the merge touched only the intended 19 marketentry/statute/doc files and zero culture-catalog files; (6) confirmed the shared orgs/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod checkout was untouched (clean, detached at its prior pin) before merging. Landed via the agent's pushed branch feature/market-entry-actor-cod -> server-side merge (gh api repos/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-iso3166-cod/merges, commit 37471ee6c63e69cf5357d0534616190cbcfc907c) -> manifest/west.yml pin advanced 8155ff8cf33f -> 37471ee6c63e (fast-forward, verified by verify-west-pins) done from an isolated worktree with a worktree-local west init. loop-system-dynamics pin was already fresh this iteration (no patch needed). Applied the commit-and-push-as-SEPARATE-Bash-calls workaround discovered in iteration 36 (the git-push-main-sync-guard hook's regex matches 'git push' anywhere in a compound command string and blocks the ENTIRE chained command atomically before any of it runs, including an earlier git commit in the same invocation).", :event/screened-out-false-positives "None this iteration (axis was prod-ready).", :event/not-done-this-iteration "No real-world-ingest-gap repo landed this iteration -- second landing of the 6-country parallel batch (BWA done, COD done, CAF/COG/COM/CPV still in flight). Axis alternation is now 19 prod-ready / 18 real-world-ingest-gap across 37 iterations.", :event/sup